  "findings": [
    "All16 contact pages inspected: eight prediction and eight GT comparison pages, covering all32 bundles. All6 selected full prediction and all6 full evaluation cases inspected.",
    "WorldFrame renders learned metric cuboids in calibrated RGB views and in isometric view; blue car and green bicycle roughly align in Town01, with visible yaw and footpoint offsets. No reconstructed mesh is shown.",
    "Town04 front/right rocks and trees produce large incorrect truck hypotheses in246933/246949, propagated from2D detections and class-size priors. A distant real red truck is also visible inTown01-01; not all unmatched truck proposals imply no truck exists in the scene.",
    "Pink pedestrian hypotheses may duplicate, shift laterally, or attach to riders. Motorcycle/bicycle classification and occlusion failures remain. Basic nearest tracking has11 ID switches over86 consecutive correctly matched transitions; no stable long-term tracking claim.",
    "GT green vs prediction orange overlays expose orientation/center errors inTown04. Validation-only results are materially worse than the known training clips. GT-crop mean yaw72deg is not reliable orientation estimation.",
    "Predicted ground patches are broader/smoother than the sparse GT surface grid, especially sloped terrain projected onto the flat plane. This is ground-plus-cuboid occupancy, not fine3D geometry. Unknown remains dark; free is ray evidence only.",
    "Endpoint voxels and the ground/below-ground slab are excluded from free carving in both final predictor and independent GT evaluator. Earlier ray/slab ambiguity is preserved in run001, not rewritten as success.",
    "Low barriers, guardrails, Fence and buildings still appear in development clips. No new full wall-free route is certified and no vehicle was driven.",
    "Same simulator assets recur across train/validation, so very small L/W errors and exact class dimension priors do not demonstrate unseen-shape learning. Bus has no positive actor/voxel support in the32-frame end-to-end pilot."
